check.check-content:
From the Microsoft Intune admin center:
1. Select Devices 2. Select Configuration 3. Select the profile which applies to the macOS device 4. Under Configuration settings heading 5. Expand the System Configuration heading 6. Under the Energy Saver subheading 7. Under Desktop Power 8. Verify that Wake on LAN is present and set to False 9. Under Laptop Battery Power 10.Verify that Wake on LAN is present and set to False 11.Under Laptop Power 12.Verify that Wake on LAN is present and set to False Or, from the device:
1. Open a Terminal 2. Run the following command to verify that a profile is installed that disables Wake On Lan is installed:
/usr/bin/sudo /usr/bin/profiles -P -o stdout | /usr/bin/grep "Wake on LAN"
3. The following output is expected:
"Wake on LAN" = 0;
"Wake on LAN" = 0;
"Wake on LAN" = 0;
Internal Only - General

From the Microsoft Intune admin center:
1. Select Devices 2. Select Configuration 3. Select the profile which applies to the macOS device 4. Under Configuration settings heading 5. Expand the System Configuration heading 6. Under the Energy Saver subheading 7. Under Desktop Power 8. Verify that Wake on Modem Ring is present and set to False 9. Under Laptop Battery Power 10.Verify that Wake on Modem Ring is present and set to False 11.Under Laptop Power 12.Verify that Wake on Modem Ring is present and set to False Or, from the device:
1. Open a Terminal 2. Run the following command to verify that a profile is installed that disables Wake On Lan is installed:
/usr/bin/sudo /usr/bin/profiles -P -o stdout | /usr/bin/grep "Wake On Modem
Ring"
3. The following output is expected:
"Wake On Modem Ring" = 0;
"Wake On Modem Ring" = 0;
"Wake On Modem Ring" = 0;
Internal Only - General
